# The Meridian Recovery agent service (examples/agent-anchored-audit,
# service mode). Built from the REPO ROOT so the @intx/* workspace
# packages resolve — the example runs from source via the intx-src
# condition, exactly like local `bun run serve`.
#
#   docker build -f Dockerfile.recovery-agent -t sanning/recovery-agent .
#   docker run -p 4610:4610 -v recovery-data:/data \
#     -e OPENROUTER_API_KEY=... -e DEMO_PASSCODE=... sanning/recovery-agent
#
# Runtime env (see examples/agent-anchored-audit/README.md):
#   PORT (Railway injects it) · SANNING_CONTEXT_DIR (defaults to /data
#   here — mount the volume there) · DEMO_PASSCODE · OPENROUTER_API_KEY
#   · SANNING_API_KEY and friends for production anchoring.

FROM oven/bun:1.2.23
WORKDIR /app

# The whole workspace: workspace deps + vendored tarballs live in-tree.
# .dockerignore keeps .git, tmp/, node_modules, and .env files out.
COPY . .

RUN bun install --frozen-lockfile

ENV NODE_ENV=production
# Persistent state (identity.json, wallet.json, anchor/ retention trail)
# lives here — mount a volume at /data. Unset SANNING_CONTEXT_DIR falls
# back to <repo>/tmp/agent-anchored-audit/context, which is ephemeral
# inside a container.
ENV SANNING_CONTEXT_DIR=/data

EXPOSE 4610
CMD ["bun", "--conditions=intx-src", "run", "examples/agent-anchored-audit/src/serve.ts"]
